<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee export problems resolved - Abecafe.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee export problems resolved - Abecafe.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Problems with Brazil's export registration system reported earlier by the Brazilian Coffee Exporters' Association (Abecafe) have now been resolved, Abecafe said in a statement.</p>
<p>Earlier today Abecafe said exporters had been unable to make new registrations, fix prices or program future shipments since April 1. Other exporter officials had said they had heard only of some delays and that shipments were continuing.</p>
<p>According to the latest Abecafe statement, the problem had been resolved this afternoon.</p>
<p>An official in Brasilia from the Internal Revenue service which runs the Siscomex system said, &quot;We do not have a single problem with Siscomex&quot;.</p>
<p>((-Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
